  "body": "https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28622 claims that window.close() during the unload and beforeunload events is non-interoperable. The specific scenario under consideration is\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<body>\r\n<script>\r\nwindow.addEventListener(\"beforeunload\", function() { window.close() }, false);\r\n</script>\r\n</body>\r\n```\r\n\r\nloaded as the first document in a browsing context.\r\n\r\nRelated issues:\r\n- #1866 \r\n- #2666\r\n- #2683",
